lesson k-food-words v=1 format=teach grade=0 unit=6 subject=language levels=[easy, medium, hard] {
  title "[[food.apple|cap]], [[food.bread]], [[food.milk]]"
  goal "Name five foods and drinks in [[language.name]]."

  look {
    scene 14x5 {
      props row count=3 prop=apple at=canvas(1, 1)
    }
    say """
        Food in [[language.name]]: an apple is [[food.apple]], bread is [[food.bread]], milk is
        [[food.milk]], water is [[food.water]] and a banana is [[food.banana]]. To ask for something,
        add [[greet.please]].
      """
  }
  do {
    level easy {
      worked k.lang-food-meaning k=0 level=medium
    }
    practice k.lang-food-meaning count=3 seed=2 easy-count=2
    practice k.lang-food-name count=2 seed=3
    practice k.lang-apples count=2 seed=4 easy-count=1
    show k.lang-ask-for-food
  }
  try stars=2 {
    show k.lang-polite-ask
  }
  try stars=3 {
    show k.lang-yellow-food k=0 hard-k=1
  }
  remember {
    say "[[food.apple|cap]], [[food.bread]], [[food.milk]], [[food.water]], [[food.banana]], and [[greet.please]] to ask."
  }

  grown-ups """
    Read every word aloud, [[food.apple]] said [[food.apple|say]], and let the child say it back;
    the child picks from what you read. One to five counted in the language; this lesson is the step
    on from it, counting apples with the number words and asking for food with [[greet.please]].
    The asking at lunch is for you to listen to. Off the page, name the food on the table in the
    language at every meal for a week. Japan, 幼稚園教育要領 (kindergarten guidelines), 言葉, 内容 (7):
    "生活の中で言葉の楽しさや美しさに気付く。" (Notice the fun and beauty of words in daily life.) The
    phrases are in [[language.variety]].
    """
  level easy {
    grown-ups "At this level apple is worked in the teacher's pen first, the foods are apple and milk, and the apples to count are one to three."
  }
  level hard {
    grown-ups "At this level the foods include bread, water and banana, the apples to count are three to five, and the three-star is about white milk."
  }
}
